    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017-sch-1-sec-57a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57A Act not to apply so as to exceed Commonwealth power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017#sch-1-sec-57a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a provision of this Act, or of an instrument made under this Act:\n\n(a) would, apart from this section, have an application (an\ninvalid application) in relation to:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments commencing on 1 July 2015  Part 1\n\nNo. 115, 2017\nAustralian Border Force Amendment (Protected Information) Act 2017\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nbecause of which the provision exceeds the Commonwealth’s\nlegislative power; but\n\n(b) also has at least one application (a valid application) in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nthat, if it were the provision’s only application, would be\nwithin the Commonwealth’s legislative power;\nit is the Parliament’s intention that the provision is not to have the\ninvalid application, but is to have every valid application.\n\n(2) This section applies to a provision of this Act, or of an instrument\nmade under this Act, whether the provision is enacted or made\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a provision of this Act, or of an instrument made under this Act:\n\n(a) would, apart from this section, have an application (an\ninvalid application) in relation to:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments commencing on 1 July 2015  Part 1\n\nNo. 115, 2017\nAustralian Border Force Amendment (Protected Information) Act 2017\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nbecause of which the provision exceeds the Commonwealth’s\nlegislative power; but\n\n(b) also has at least one application (a valid application) in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nthat, if it were the provision’s only application, would be\nwithin the Commonwealth’s legislative power;\nit is the Parliament’s intention that the provision is not to have the\ninvalid application, but is to have every valid application.\n\n(2) This section applies to a provision of this Act, or of an instrument\nmade under this Act, whether the provision is enacted or made\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017-sch-1-sec-57a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017-sch-1-sec-57a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a15ad528e47b702271b9a8feefcc56977e2660c676c56c5aa887ff1676f73c24"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-border-force-amendment-protected-information-act-2017#sch-1-sec-57a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57A Act not to apply so as to exceed Commonwealth power",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a provision of this Act, or of an instrument made under this Act:\n\n(a) would, apart from this section, have an application (an\ninvalid application) in relation to:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments commencing on 1 July 2015  Part 1\n\nNo. 115, 2017\nAustralian Border Force Amendment (Protected Information) Act 2017\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nbecause of which the provision exceeds the Commonwealth’s\nlegislative power; but\n\n(b) also has at least one application (a valid application) in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) one or more particular persons, things, matters, places,\ncircumstances or cases; or\n\n(ii) one or more classes (however defined or determined) of\npersons, things, matters, places, circumstances or cases;\n\nthat, if it were the provision’s only application, would be\nwithin the Commonwealth’s legislative power;\nit is the Parliament’s intention that the provision is not to have the\ninvalid application, but is to have every valid application.\n\n(2) This section applies to a provision of this Act, or of an instrument\nmade under this Act, whether the provision is enacted or made\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this section."
    },
